&#xD;
A Study on the Sustainability of the Contractor&#xD;
&#xD;
&#xD;
Nam, Sung Kyu&#xD;
(Supervisor Park, Sung Yong)&#xD;
Dept. of Housing City Management&#xD;
Graduate School of Housing City&#xD;
Seoul National University of Science and Technology&#xD;
&#xD;
&#xD;
As we can, see the unfair activities of large multinational corporation and me-too movement, the unfairness culture(“bossing culture”) taking advantage of their superiority position is prevalent and this problem is also recognized as an important topic in the construction area too. &#xD;
Despite that the cooperative and horizontal relationship between contractor(A) and sub-contractor(B) in the construction business is important, there are still many unfair practices such as low contraction cost, requirement for shorter construction period, unfair request for command compliance, payment pressure for B in case of loss, A employees’intervention. This power balance problem between A and B could be A’s problem but sometimes it could be due to B, therefore, the power balance and conflict problems exist. &#xD;
Based on this, we hypothesized that the B who are having continuous transaction will have higher satisfaction than the one who discontinued its transaction. That is, longer relationship implies higher satisfaction and shorter relationship implies lower satisfaction.&#xD;
That does not mean that keeping the relationship has higher satisfaction and financial loss or low profit ratio leads to lower satisfaction. Namely, we hypothesize that in case that big burden to B and discontinuation of transaction will lead to higher satisfaction than keeping the transaction.   &#xD;
Empirical analysis shows that keeping transaction has higher satisfaction than discontinuation and for economic, future prospect, human aspects, higher satisfaction will result in and for forceful and uneconomic cases, lower satisfaction will lead to discontinuation of transaction.  &#xD;
Second, for the burden to B, discontinuation of traction could be better than keeping the relationship. Empirical analysis shows that in case of economic and financial loss, the forceful relationship of A and B leads to discontinuation of transaction. &#xD;
Even in the possible continuation of transaction, sometimes B might voluntarily withdraw their relationship. &#xD;
In this research, we investigated the longer relationship between A and B and examined how to develop the better relationship and form the partnership, enhance quality of construction. and propose more sound culture in the construction business.&#xD;
